1
00:07:55,199 --> 00:08:01,199
The world of Pandora will change forever.

2
00:15:50,399 --> 00:15:56,399
Avatar: Fire and Ash is a science fiction, adventure,
fantasy film directed by James Cameron.

3
00:23:45,599 --> 00:23:51,599
In the wake of the devastating war against the RDA and the loss of their eldest son, Jake Sully and Neytiri face a new
threat on Pandora: the Ash People, a violent and power-hungry Na'vi tribe led by the ruthless Varang.

4
00:31:40,799 --> 00:31:46,799
Jake's family must fight for their survival and the future of Pandora in a
conflict that pushes them to their emotional and physical limits.

5
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Jake, played by Sam Worthington.

6
00:47:31,199 --> 00:47:37,199
Neytiri, played by Zoe Saldaña.

7
00:55:26,400 --> 00:55:32,400
Kiri, played by Sigourney Weaver.

8
01:03:21,599 --> 01:03:27,599
Quaritch, played by Stephen Lang.

9
01:11:16,800 --> 01:11:22,800
Varang, played by Oona Chaplin.

10
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
Spider, played by Jack Champion.

11
01:27:07,199 --> 01:27:13,199
Avatar: Fire and Ash is a 2025 American epic science fiction film directed by
James Cameron, and written by Cameron, Rick Jaffa and Amanda Silver.

12
01:35:02,399 --> 01:35:08,399
It is the third in the Avatar film series, and features Sam Worthington, Zoe Saldaña, Sigourney Weaver, Stephen Lang
and Kate Winslet reprising their roles from the previous films, with Oona Chaplin joining the cast.

13
01:42:57,599 --> 01:43:03,599
It follows the human-turned-Na'vi Jake Sully and his family on the habitable moon Pandora, as they face the combined
threat of the human RDA forces and the Mangkwan, a tribe of ruthless, warmongering, collaborationist Na'vi.

14
01:50:52,800 --> 01:50:58,800
Cameron, who had stated in mid-2006 that he would like to make sequels to Avatar (2009) if it was successful, announced the first
two sequels in early 2010 following the success of the first film, with Avatar 3 aiming for a December 2015 release.

15
01:58:48,000 --> 01:58:54,000
However, the addition of two further sequels, and the development of new technology required to film performance capture scenes underwater, a feat never
accomplished before, led to significant delays to allow the crew more time to work on the writing, pre-production, and visual effects.

16
02:06:43,199 --> 02:06:49,199
The film started shooting simultaneously with Avatar: The Way
of Water in New Zealand on September 25, 2017.

17
02:14:38,399 --> 02:14:44,399
Filming completed in late December 2020, after over three years of shooting.

18
02:22:33,600 --> 02:22:39,600
With an estimated production budget of at least $350 million, it
is one of the most expensive films ever made.

19
02:30:28,799 --> 02:30:34,799
Avatar: Fire and Ash had its world premiere at Dolby Theatre in Hollywood, on December 1, 2025,
and was released in the United States on December 19 by 20th Century Studios.

20
02:38:24,000 --> 02:38:30,000
Critical response was generally positive, with praise for the visual effects and
spectacle, but complaints that it repeats the narrative beats of its predecessors.

21
02:46:19,199 --> 02:46:25,199
It grossed $1.379 billion worldwide, becoming the
third-highest grossing film of 2025.

22
02:54:14,399 --> 02:54:20,399
Named among the top ten films of 2025 by the American Film Institute and the National Board of Review, it received two Academy Award (Best Visual Effects and Best Costume Design) and
two Golden Globe Award nominations, and has two planned sequels, Avatar 4 and Avatar 5, production of which is dependent on the box-office performance of Fire and Ash.

23
03:02:09,600 --> 03:02:15,600
The film explores themes of witch, clone, space war, tribe, sequel.

24
03:10:04,799 --> 03:10:10,799
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and emotional.
